    "intro": "Every enzyme in this topic — amylase, pepsin, trypsin, lipase, maltase — is a protein acting as a <b>biological catalyst</b>: it increases the rate of a reaction and is <b>not changed</b> by it. Each has an <b>optimum</b> temperature and pH; far from the optimum it is <b>denatured</b>.",
    "open": "Open the recap: the three graphs, described the way the mark scheme wants",
